// **The method comes from the derive, not from the shape.** A type that does not derive the trait
// has no `to_string`, no `eq` and no `compare`, and each is refused where it is written.
//
// The membership half agrees: `traits_of` on this type is empty and `x is dyn Display` is `false`,
// so refusing the call is the same answer said twice — which is exactly what a derived implementor
// gets the other way round (see `derive_builtin_method_doors`). Without this, "the method is
// installed" could pass by installing it on every nominal type.
//
// Two things separate this from a runtime abort raising the same code at the same spans. The two
// `echo`s come FIRST and expect nothing on stdout — a run reaching the calls would have printed
// them — and three diagnostics come out of one run, where a run aborts at the first bad call.

// expect: error E0007 at 24:6
// expect: error E0007 at 25:6
// expect: error E0007 at 26:6
// expect: exit 1

struct Plain {
    n: int
}

echo traits_of(Plain { n: 1 })
echo Plain { n: 1 } is dyn Display
echo Plain { n: 1 }.to_string()
echo Plain { n: 1 }.eq(Plain { n: 1 })
echo Plain { n: 1 }.compare(Plain { n: 2 })
